cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CAIDE, please cite the software paper below."
title: "CAIDE: Cost-Aware Inference Deployment Evaluator"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for cost, energy and carbon planning of large language
  model services. CAIDE derives efficiency multipliers from a roofline
  model of the transformed deployment state rather than assuming published
  constants, decomposes total cost of ownership into six layers with
  distinct scaling laws, locates every break-even volume between candidate
  architectures, and propagates input uncertainty to a sensitivity ranking.
